# Table of contents: one entry per heading, with its title, a dot leader and its page, styled with TOC 1 to TOC 3.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Table of contents · Headings
	Page:
		Paper: A5
		Margin: 15mm
	Styles:
		For element: TOC 1
			Typography:
				Bold: true
			Box:
				Margin: 6 0 2 0
		For element: TOC 2
			Box:
				Padding: 0 0 0 14
				Margin: 0 0 2 0
		For element: TOC 3
			Typography:
				Color: muted
			Box:
				Padding: 0 0 0 28
				Margin: 0 0 2 0
	Section:
		Text: Table of contents
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			In table of contents: false
			Text: Headings
		Paragraph: A `Table of contents` lists the headings of the document in order, with the page where each one starts. Each entry leads to its heading. By default it lists levels 1 to 3, and `For element: TOC 1` to `TOC 3` style them, with the indent in the left `Padding`.
			Style: intro
		Text: Contents
			Style: contents
		Table of contents:
	Section:
		Heading 1:
			Text: Installation
		Heading 2:
			Text: Before starting
		Paragraph: Check that the box holds the thermostat, the base and four screws.
		Heading 2:
			Text: Wiring
		Heading 3:
			Text: Cables
		Paragraph: Connect the live wire to terminal L and the neutral to terminal N.
		Heading 3:
			Text: Boiler
		Paragraph: Terminals C and NO switch the boiler.
	Section:
